task.bug."https://medium.com/@chrisdunlop_37984/so-shall-we-give-up-then-2d095fa8c410" (completed) {
  bug: similar to task.bug."https://medium.com/@RetroTechShow/1993-before-mp3-and-spotify-the-bizarre-90s-battle-between-three-digital-audio-formats-4a3ba7a4f8ce", news not loading properly

  Root cause:
  The story was listed without a body because its first article fetch hit
  Medium's 403 page and the reader-mirror request transiently failed. The
  empty result was cached for an hour, so every later /news and /medium
  request (and the detail modal, which uses the already-streamed story) kept
  showing only the Google News headline. Other Medium entries had the same
  stale empty cache entries (for example the Cherry Red Cybertruck story).

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Medium is now a full-article source for both the static site:medium.com
    feed and the dynamic /medium author feed, so a feed preview is never
    trusted as the complete body.
  - Reader-mirror recovery now retries each mirror URL twice, also retries a
    tracking-parameter-free URL (Medium feeds append ?source=rss-...), and
    keeps an empty mirror result out of the long-lived cache path.
  - Empty cached bodies for reader-mirror publishers expire after 120 seconds
    instead of one hour, and a detail request explicitly ignores an empty
    cached failure so the next attempt can recover.
  - Added `news_fetch.php --json --article <url>` for fetching one article
    body on demand.
  app/chat_server.py
  - Added GET /api/news_article?url=<article_url>, which runs the on-demand
    article fetch and returns the paragraphs and images as JSON.
  app/chat.html
  - When a completed story opens in the detail modal without paragraphs, the
    modal now fetches the body on demand, shows a "loading full article…"
    state, and fills the same story in place. Reopening retries a transient
    failure instead of leaving the article permanently empty.

  Verified:
  - `./news_fetch.php --json --article` loads 31 paragraphs / 6,993 characters
    for the reported URL and 25 paragraphs / 4,904 characters for the other
    previously-cached-empty Medium story, both with cover images.
  - A cold-cache `--source medium --limit 8` run loads every story, including
    the reported one, through the reader mirror.
  - `php -l`, the Python compile check, and `node --check` on the browser
    script all pass.
}

task.bug."https://medium.com/@RetroTechShow/1993-before-mp3-and-spotify-the-bizarre-90s-battle-between-three-digital-audio-formats-4a3ba7a4f8ce" (completed) {
  similar to task.bug."https://medium.com/@adnanmasood/when-llms-edit-other-llms-weight-space-programming-and-the-conditions-for-recursive-2dceaec05403", news not loading properly

  apply systematic fix to in both news article modal and /medium command

  Root cause:
  Medium's author RSS feed (used by /medium) exposes only a short excerpt and
  a "Continue reading on Medium »" link, unlike Google News items, which have
  no body at all. storyNeedsArticleContent() treated any non-empty feed body as
  complete, so the preview was shown and the full article was never fetched in
  the detail modal or /medium. The continuation line was also rendered as a
  story paragraph.

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added feedBodyIsPreview(): detects publisher-preview bodies from a
    "Continue reading", "Read the full story", or "Read on" continuation
    marker, including in the raw feed HTML before boilerplate filtering.
  - RSS parsing now records an internal feed_preview flag, and
    storyNeedsArticleContent() forces article enrichment when it is set.
  - Added the continuation-line patterns to isBoilerplate() so a leftover
    preview line is never emitted as article prose.
  - The existing Medium reader-mirror fallback then loads the complete body, so
    the same fix covers the /news detail modal (Google News Medium items) and
    the /medium command without source-specific branching.

  Verified:
  - `HOME=<temp> news_fetch.php --json --source medium_author --limit 3` with
    @RetroTechShow now emits 84-106 paragraphs / 15-24k characters per story
    (including the reported 1993 DAT/DCC/MiniDisc article) instead of one
    38-75 character teaser paragraph.
  - The reported medium.com URL still loads through /googlenews and the
    reader mirror; php -l passes.
}

task.bug."https://medium.com/@adnanmasood/when-llms-edit-other-llms-weight-space-programming-and-the-conditions-for-recursive-2dceaec05403" (completed) {
  bug: simplier to task.bug."https://www.axios.com/2026/11/09/alice-huang-nvidia-jensen-megaspeed", news not loading properly

  Root cause:
  Medium serves article pages behind a Cloudflare bot challenge (HTTP 403),
  and unlike Axios its public author feed (https://medium.com/feed/@user)
  carries only a short description, not the story body, so the existing feed
  fallback could not recover the article.

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added ARTICLE_READER_FALLBACKS and fetchArticleReaderFallback(). When a
    fetched article page yields no readable paragraphs, a publisher-specific
    public reader mirror is tried as a last resort after the feed fallback.
    For medium.com the mirror is https://freedium-mirror.cfd/{url}, which
    renders the complete story even though the page itself is challenged.
  - Reader-mirror bodies reuse the normal paragraph and image extractors. The
    mirror URL is passed as the base URL so relative image paths resolve
    through the mirror's image proxy instead of the blocked publisher host.
  - Bumped ARTICLE_EXTRACTOR_VERSION to 5 so previously cached empty Medium
    entries are refetched instead of being served from the failure cache.

  Verified: the reported URL now streams 122 paragraphs / 37,744 characters
  (subtitle, TL;DR, every section, and all 30 references) plus its lead image.
  Other Adnan Masood Medium stories in the same Google News batch also load
  their complete bodies; php -l and the server Python syntax check pass.
}

task.bug."https://www.axios.com/2026/11/09/alice-huang-nvidia-jensen-megaspeed" (completed) {
  bug: similar to task.bug."https://en.fnnews.com/news/202611071101376017", news not loading properly

  Root cause:
  Axios serves its article pages behind a Cloudflare bot challenge (HTTP 403),
  so extractArticleParagraphs() received only the "Just a moment..." page and
  cached an empty body for the story.

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added ARTICLE_FEED_FALLBACKS and fetchArticleFeedFallback(). When a fetched
    article page yields no readable paragraphs (for example a bot challenge),
    the publisher's public RSS feed is fetched once per batch and the matching
    item is located by canonical URL.
    Axios publishes the complete story (paragraphs, bullets, section headings,
    and lead image) in https://api.axios.com/feed/, so its full text is restored
    without bypassing the site's protection with a scraper.
  - Feed bodies are parsed in document order from p, li, and h2-h4 elements,
    with the same CSS/boilerplate/duplicate filtering as page extraction.
  - Bumped ARTICLE_EXTRACTOR_VERSION to 4 so previously cached empty Axios
    entries are refetched.

  Verified: /googlenews "site:axios.com alice huang jensen" now emits 37
  paragraphs (5,477 characters) for the reported URL, including every section
  and bullet, plus the lead image. Other Axios stories in the same batch also
  load their full bodies; php -l passes.
}

task.bug."https://en.fnnews.com/news/202611071101376017" (completed) {
  in the news popup, it failed to load the full text content of "https://en.fnnews.com/news/202611071101376017"

  Root cause:
  Financial News English renders the article body inside div#textSize.view_cont
  as bare text separated by <br> tags, with no <p> elements at all, so the
  paragraph-only extractor returned zero paragraphs.

  Implemented:
  news_fetch.php
  - Added collectLineSegmentNodes(), which walks a semantic body container and
    collects prose split by <br> and block elements while keeping inline markup
    in its line. It skips scripts, styles, ads, sharing controls, related-story
    rails, navigation, sidebars, footers, and bylines.
  - extractArticleParagraphs() now also evaluates semantic containers
    (articleBody, article-body, paragraphs-container, <article>, article/content
    classes, view_cont, <main>) with the line-segment collector. Existing <p>
    extraction still comes first, so sites with normal paragraphs are unchanged.
  - Bumped ARTICLE_EXTRACTOR_VERSION to 3 so previously cached partial bodies
    are refetched.

  Verified: the reported URL now extracts 18 paragraphs / 3,773 characters
  (headline, intro, every body section, and the closing ETF section) plus its
  lead image. NPR (50 paragraphs / 10,179 chars), CBC Lite (17 paragraphs /
  3,951 chars), and The Infatuation guide (39 paragraphs / 9,048 chars) still
  extract their complete bodies. php -l passes.
}

