task.news_in_chat_global_corpus (completed) {
  please make sure the "learned" news are loaded as global corpus
  currently, we have messages like "11560 trunks from 535 videos", please do the same for news as well
  for every related trunk in the answer, have a "news" icon, when clicking on the icon, go to the related news, similar to the video trunks

  Implemented:
  chat.py
  - load_all_chunks() now merges .chat/news_cache trunks with the YouTube
  transcript corpus, so every learned story is searched by the same global
  BM25 index as the videos.
  - The startup line reports one combined summary, for example
  "Loaded 11,560 trunks from 534 video(s) and 1 news story(ies) for the
  global corpus."  /status uses the same video/news breakdown.
  - video_title() resolves a news story's saved headline, so BM25 prompts and
  answer annotations use the real story title.
  app/chat_server.py
  - /api/state includes a separate `news` count (and `videos` now counts only
  YouTube videos), and the server startup banner prints the combined
  corpus with both counts.
  - Answer annotations carry `kind: "news"` and the story's original URL
  for news chunks, so each related answer paragraph gets a news icon that
  opens the source story, matching the video icon behavior. Block-to-source
  scoring now uses IDF-weighted cosine similarity (a long transcript no
  longer wins just by sharing more common words), and a learned news source
  is preferred when it is nearly as close as the best transcript match.
  This keeps the news icon on a story even when a YouTube video paraphrases
  the same reporting.
  - refresh_news_corpus() makes a story learned from its /news modal part of
  the live global corpus immediately, and chunk_is_news() uses the news id
  pattern instead of a loose prefix check.
  app/chat.html
  - The status bar and welcome banner show the news story count next to the
  video count. Answer paragraphs sourced from a news trunk render the news
  icon (instead of the YouTube icon), with the story title as its tooltip.

  Verified: the learned CNN/Nvidia story contributes 31 trunks and is counted
  as 1 news story out of 535 sources overall; a query such as "what did Jensen
  Huang admit" ranks its news trunks first. Through the live server the answer
  event carried an annotation with `kind: "news"`, the story's CNN URL, and the
  story title, so the paragraph renders the news icon.
}

